UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 4, Week 10, Lesson 3: Estimating products', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Estimating products by rounding factors checks whether an exact answer is reasonable before or after calculating.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same method to a larger number or a new context, then compare two solution paths for accuracy.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nEstimate 73 × 4 and say whether 292 is reasonable.\n\nFEEDBACK\nAbout 70 × 4 = 280; 292 is reasonable/close.\n\nWATCH FOR\nEstimating with the wrong place (e.g. rounding 48 to 40 when a nearer estimate helps) can still work if you judge closeness carefully.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nFor twelve multiplications, write an estimate, compute exactly and mark close/far with a reason for six.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Mathematics","learning_intention":"Estimating products by rounding factors checks whether an exact answer is reasonable before or after calculating.","lesson_number":3,"lesson_role":"Problem solving","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: place-value chart or number line"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["MA2-MR-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: For twelve multiplications, write an estimate, compute exactly and mark close/far with a reason for six. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: new numbers solved with visible working for estimate; key places/v