nd name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing only the final answer without working does not show the method. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Show the working","visual":[{"alt":"Estimate quality notes.","caption":"Twelve estimate–exact pairs.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Close/far</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">mark six</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Risk</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">no estimate</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison.","options":["Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no working"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about estimate with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nEstimating with the wrong place (e.g. rounding 48 to 40 when a nearer estimate helps) can still work if you judge closeness carefully. Here is a more productive model: Estimate 48 × 6 ≈ 50 × 6 = 300. Exact 288 is close. An exact answer of 88 would be unreasonable.\n\nTRY FIRST\nDescribe why the warned-against approach gives the wrong value or meaning, then write corrected working.\n\nFEEDBACK\n